// P3B.2 / A15: "Exercise: Pneumatic Cylinder" (intro-to-assemblies.md A15, ex2-step1..20) on the
// stand-in `fixtures/pneumatic_cylinder_standin.cadrs` (intro-to-assemblies-gaps.md "Ex2
// Pneumatic Cylinder"), every step through the UI. The mates pick circular edges (their centre
// is their only implicit point, A6.6); the stand-in has no O-ring grooves, so the O-rings go on
// the spigots' edges with offsets instead (the same end state; asserted in
// cadrs_core/tests/course_pneumatic.rs).
// 01 (A15.1, ex2-step1) the copied document: Part Studio "Cylinder parts", 9 parts, inch / pound.
// 02 (A15.2, ex2-step2) + → Create Assembly, renamed "Cylinder assembly".
// 03 (A15.3, ex2-step3) Insert: Barrel, Rear Cap, Retaining Plate, Top Cap picked in turn with the
//    pointer in the dialog (studio positions); 04 accepted.
// 05 (A15.4, ex2-step4) right-click Barrel <1> → Fix; 06 the fixed icon.
// 07 (A15.5, ex2-step5) Group with the four instances; 08 "Group 1" in Mate Features.
// 09 (A15.6, ex2-step6) the Rear Cap mount clicked into the graphics area.
// 10 (A15.7, ex2-step7) Revolute: the Rear Cap's recess edge (from below), then the mount's top
//    edge: the mount swivels under the cap (the implicit points show on the hovered edge).
// 11 (A15.8, ex2-step8) four O-Ring 0.125 clicked in.
// 12 (A15.9, ex2-step9) Barrel hidden; Fastened 1: the O-ring's top edge on the Rear Cap spigot's
//    base edge, primary axis flipped.
// 13 (A15.10, ex2-step10) Fastened 2–4 (Offset Z −0.25 in on the spigot's top edge; two under the
//    Top Cap, seen from below, the second with Offset Z 0.25 in).
// 14 (A15.11, ex2-step11) a Structural Rod clicked in.
// 15 (A15.12, ex2-step12) Fastened 5: the rod's top edge on a flange hole's edge, Offset Z 0.5 in.
// 16 (A15.13, ex2-step13) right-click the rod → Copy Structural Rod <1>; 17 right-click empty
//    space → Paste Structural Rod <1> (three times).
// 18 (A15.14, ex2-step14) Fastened 6–8 (the last one's dialog open).
// 19 (A15.15, ex2-step15) the Piston & Rod clicked in.
// 20 (A15.16, ex2-step16) Slider: the piston's bottom edge, then the Rear Cap spigot's top edge;
//    Limits Z −3.25 in … 0 in.
// 21 (A15.17, ex2-step17) three O-Ring 0.185 clicked in.
// 22 (A15.18, ex2-step18) Fastened 9–11, the last one accepted: 17 instances, 14 mates.
// 23 right-click Slider 1 → Apply limit position ▸ Z minimum; 24 the piston at its top: Mass
//    properties CoM z 3.990 in.
// 25 (A15.19, ex2-step19) right-click Slider 1 → Reset; 26 (A15.20, ex2-step20) the top-level
//    assembly's Mass properties: 2.853 lb, 20.624 in³, CoM (0.000, 0.000, 3.167) in.
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
